, -2949.59), `eighteenth_prairie` (1401.86, -3206.93) and `cermak_prairie` (1407.06, -3764.87) are the three junctions the ticket named, resolved from OpenStreetMap under the same node rule the street control uses and recorded with their node ids in data/traces/south_anchor_control.json. `battle_reach_1812` (1460, -3050) stands on the shore between the first two, looking north back up the beach toward the fort. IT DOES NOT LOCATE THE BATTLE, and its label says so: it names the ZONE T-0470 mapped (data/terrain/1812_evacuation_route.geojson, derived by tools/derive_evacuation_1812.py), which runs from the north end of Heald's 'about a mile and a half' band to Eighteenth Street's south line because the distance and the Eighteenth Street tradition disagree by about a kilometre and the zone spans both rather than choosing. The anchor stands inside that zone near its south end, 157 m north of Eighteenth Street's row, and claims no point in it. Until T-0470 it was labelled 'not yet located', because an anchor that named a spot before the zone was mapped would have been this scene inventing the very thing that ticket existed to adjudicate. WHAT THE LABELS MAY SAY. An anchor name describes what the SELECTED YEAR contains, so two of these carry `conjectural ground` and one carries `the model's south wall`: below Twelfth Street nothing in this corpus states the land at all \\u2014 the terrain spec's `evidence_limit` writes every vertex down there conjectural \\u2014 and a viewpoint that said otherwise would be a claim the ground cannot carry. The modern street names are LOCATORS and are marked as such by being modern; they assert no 1835 street, and the structure layer is offset from none of them. Anchors live in the scene file, one per year, so a later epoch gets its own list rather than inheriting these \\u2014 which is the mechanism that keeps an 1880s mansion out of an 1812 label. tools/measure_anchors.mjs holds all seventeen against the heightfield every anchor is meant to stand on, and tools/check.sh runs it.\",\n+  \"static_support_regions\": [\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"western_hotel_yard_horse_support_01\",\n+      \"record_id\": \"western_hotel_wagon_yard\",\n+      \"bounds_enu_m\": [\n+        [\n+          -128.08635326139702,\n+          -296.39700380717545\n+        ],\n+        [\n+          -126.99391406043152,\n+          -295.6039917788591\n+        ]\n+      ],\n+      \"basis\": \"Unchanged canonical neutral hoof contact annotations after declared rigid support/heading, with50mm plan margin. Canonical metre derivative uses unit runtime scale; source/pose changes outside this region refuse support.\",\n+      \"maximum_region_count\": 1,\n+      \"maximum_region_area_m2\": 4,\n+      \"maximum_retained_triangles\": 32,\n+      \"maximum_retained_typed_array_bytes\": 4096,\n+      \"lifetime\": \"Snapshot actual drawn yard triangles before upload release; own only narrow Float64 triangle copies until yards.dispose, normal original arrays still release.\"\n+    }\n+  ]\n }"},{"sha":"321de8d5b706ddc49d23393720924fed03d4fc26","filename":"chicago/4d/data/sidecars/1812/sources/uses.json","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changes":2,"blob_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/blob/fa115d72534e234fe5ac7b94fd2f1a3eb38065c8/chicago%2F4d%2Fdata%2Fsidecars%2F1812%2Fsources%2Fuses.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago/raw/fa115d72534e234fe5ac7b94fd2f1a3eb38065c8/chicago%2F4d%2Fdata%2Fsidecars%2F1812%2Fsources%2Fuses.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/contents/chicago%2F4d%2Fdata%2Fsidecars%2F1812%2Fsources%2Fuses.json?ref=fa115d72534e234fe5ac7b94fd2f1a3eb38065c8","patch":"@@ -1 +1 @@\n-{\"catalog\":\"1835\",\"scene\":\"1812\",\"schema_version\":1,\"uses\":{\"alvord_street_paving_report_1904\":\"other_scene\",\"andreas_1884_chicago_1830_map\":\"other_scene\",\"andreas_1884_dearborn_drawbridge_plate\":\"unused\",\"andreas_1884_green_tree_hotel_plate\":\"unused\"